[  215.6s] - **callback**: not decided. The brief has no callback rules, so the defaults apply.
[  215.6s] - **identity.questions**: supported. "Ask for the postcode first, then the year of birth. Send the postcode in capital letters with exactly one space before the last three characters … Send the year of birth as four digits." The fields `postcode` (upper, space_before_last:3) and `birth_year` (year) match the API enum.
[  215.6s] - **identity.max_wrong**: supported. "The identity check has failed at the second wrong answer in total, across both questions." The API agrees ("Two wrong answers in total end the check"), so 2 is right. The email's "three goes?" is overridden by the policy.
[  215.6s] - **identity.hints**: supported. The API returns no hint values, so the empty map is right.
[  215.6s] - **identity** (rest): supported. The response fields `ok`, `verified`, `wrong_answers_left` and `all_verified` match the API.
[  215.6s] - **products.amount_field / days_field**: supported. These are `arrears` ("amount overdue in pounds") and `days_overdue`. Also `list_field` products, `id_field` ref, `type_field` product_type.
[  215.6s] - **products.floor_field**: supported. "Personal loan: the monthly instalment in bands A and B" maps to `instalment`.
[  215.6s] - **products.floor_pct**: supported. Card 15%. Overdraft is 20% because memo item 4 says "Overdraft floor: 20% of the arrears instead of 25%."
[  215.6s] - **products** (rest): supported. Rounding is up:5 for the card and up:10 for the overdraft. Minimums are 30 and 50, and the floor is capped at the arrears. `promise_scale` is 100 because the API says "Promised amount in whole pence (integer)". In band C the loan floor is the full arrears (`floor_full_types`).
[  215.6s] - **bands**: supported.
[  215.6s]   - Band A is days 1–20, deadline the 5th business day after today, 3 attempts. Memo item 1: "Band A deadline is now the 5th business day after today."
[  215.6s]   - Band B is days 21–60, deadline the last business day of the month, 4 attempts. "If today is itself the last business day of the month (or later)" means the computed date is today or earlier, which is what `roll_if_not_after_today` does.
[  215.6s]   - Band C is days 61 and over, deadline the 2nd business day after today, 3 attempts.
[  215.6s] - **ladder**: supported. Step 1 is "full today", because "the opening 'everything today' question counts as attempt 1". Then full on the 2nd business day, full on the deadline, and the floor on the deadline. These are policy 2.6 steps 1–3, in order.
[  215.6s] - **notes**: supported. "Every product that ends without a promise gets one note."
[  215.6s] - **events**: supported. "Transfers close as `handed_over` with reason `hardship`, `plans` or `general`." Identity closes as `id_not_passed` with `failed` or `declined`. Notes come from the CL-12 per-type codes. Three things are invented and recorded as assumptions, because `close_call` requires a reason and the brief gives none: the `service_error` reason (`system_error`) and the not-reached reasons. The `N-SYS` note comes from "System failure on any product (a tool fails twice)".
[  215.6s] - **tool_bodies**: supported. Every required request field in the API is mapped. `add_note.code` maps to n_reason.
[  215.6s] - **multi**: supported. "These end that product only: write the note and carry on with the remaining products." The close order needs handling order, which no field can carry, so it is correctly listed as unsupported.
